{"type":"message","id":"234dd52b","parentId":"c4a7a9e8","timestamp":"2026-05-14T12:31:51.238Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.exec:33","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw agent --agent writer --message \"First, read the COINOGRAPHY_TEMPLATE.md file in your workspace to learn your strict formatting rules. Then, write a 1100-1200 word crypto news article using these facts: {\\\"topic_theme\\\": \\\"Bitcoin ETFs Shed \\$630M in Largest Daily Exit Since January\\\", \\\"primary_keyword\\\": \\\"Bitcoin ETF Outflows\\\", \\\"primary_headline\\\": \\\"Bitcoin ETFs Bleed \\$630M in Record Daily Outflow Since January as Inflation Fears Trigger Institutional Retreat\\\", \\\"sources_used\\\": [\\\"Decrypt\\\", \\\"CoinTelegraph\\\", \\\"Google News\\\"], \\\"source_urls\\\": [\\\"https://decrypt.co/367822/bitcoin-etfs-shed-630m-in-largest-daily-exit-since-january\\\", \\\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/jpmorgan-bitcoin-etf-buy-blackrock-ibit-q1-2026\\\", \\\"https://news.google.com/rss/search?q=bitcoin+crypto&hl=en-US&gl=US&ceid=US:en\\\"], \\\"combined_key_facts\\\": [\\\"U.S. spot Bitcoin ETFs recorded \\$630.4 million in net outflows on May 13, 2026 - the largest daily exit in over three months\\\", \\\"BlackRock's IBIT bore the brunt with \\$284.7 million in redemptions\\\", \\\"ARK Invest's ARKB shed \\$177.1 million, Fidelity's FBTC lost \\$133.2 million, and Bitwise's BITB exited \\$35.4 million\\\", \\\"The outflow reverses a five-week inflow streak that had pulled in roughly \\$3.8 billion in cumulative net inflows\\\", \\\"Previous largest single-day outflow was \\$817.8 million on January 29, 2026\\\", \\\"April CPI came in at 3.8%, above expectations and the highest reading since September 2023\\\", \\\"PPI print came in at 6%, the highest since February 2023\\\", \\\"Analyst Illia Otychenko from CEX.IO stated inflation data triggered broad risk aversion which 'by extension hit Bitcoin and caused elevated ETF outflows'\\\", \\\"Bitcoin was trading at \\$79,540 at time of writing, down 1.6% in the last 24 hours after briefly touching \\$82,000 over the weekend\\\", \\\"Analyst Peter Chung from Presto Labs characterized the activity as 'healthy consolidation' driven by profit-taking from a diverse institutional base\\\", \\\"The move reflects profit-taking and positioning shifts rather than a structural drop in institutional demand\\\", \\\"Rising bearish derivatives positioning noted: increased deleveraging of long positions and rising put/call options ratio\\\", \\\"Energy costs and Strait of Hormuz developments cited as additional potential volatility factors\\\", \\\"Myriad prediction market shows 84% chance of Bitcoin moving to \\$84,000 versus collapsing to \\$55,000\\\"], \\\"aggregated_raw_content\\\": \\\"U.S. spot Bitcoin ETFs bled \\$630.4 million on Wednesday, the worst single-day outflow in over three months, as back-to-back inflation shocks drove a sharp institutional retreat from risk assets. The outflows mark a dramatic reversal from the five-week inflow streak that had pulled in roughly \\$3.8 billion in cumulative net inflows through the week ending May 6. BlackRock's IBIT bore the brunt with \\$284.7 million in redemptions, while ARK Invest's ARKB shed \\$177.1 million, Fidelity's FBTC lost \\$133.2 million, and Bitwise's BITB exited \\$35.4 million, together accounting for the entirety of the day's losses. The previous largest single-day outflow was \\$817.8 million on January 29, according to Farside Investors data. The catalyst for this institutional exodus was this week's U.S. inflation data, which significantly shifted market expectations around Federal Reserve policy. April's CPI came in at 3.8%, above expectations and the highest reading since September 2023, followed a day later by a PPI print of 6%, the highest since February 2023. Together, these releases strengthened concerns that the Federal Reserve may consider rate hikes this year. Analysts note that while the headline figure appears alarming, institutions are a diverse bunch, and the resulting higher prices from bullish sentiment served as a strong incentive for another cohort of investors to lock in profits. This activity is characterized as healthy consolidation rather than a structural drop in institutional demand. Technical indicators show increased deleveraging of long positions and a rising put/call options ratio, both suggesting bearish sentiment has been increasingly building. Much will now depend on oil prices and developments around the Strait of Hormuz, with any prolonged disruption potentially pushing energy costs higher and adding another inflationary wave, increasing pressure on crypto markets. The CLARITY Act hearing outcome could also introduce additional volatility across the sector.\\\"} . You MUST finish the article completely, ending with the Sources and Word Count block.\" --deliver > /tmp/crypto-article.md","timeout":300}},{"type":"text","text":""}],"api":"bedrock-converse-stream","provider":"amazon-bedrock","model":"moonshotai.kimi-k2.5","usage":{"input":20579,"output":1124,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":21703,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778761899733}}
